  "rules": {
    "oracle": "Sneak {2}{W}{B} (You may cast this spell for {2}{W}{B} if you also return an unblocked attacker you control to hand during the declare blockers step. She enters tapped and attacking.)\nWhenever Karai deals combat damage to a player, return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand. If her sneak cost was paid this turn, instead return that card to the battlefield.",
    "cr": [
      "702.190a",
      "702.190b",
      "510.3a",
      "603.2",
      "608.2b",
      "608.2c",
      "611.2a"
    ],
    "actual": "The coverage report lists the card as unsupported with one gap, `Swallow:Duration_ThisTurn` (\"Whenever Karai deals combat damage to a player, return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand. If her sneak cost was paid thi…\"): it claims the parser dropped the clause's \"this turn\".",
    "expected": "Whenever Karai deals combat damage to a player, the targeted creature card in her controller's graveyard returns to hand; if her sneak cost was paid during the current turn, it is put onto the battlefield instead. A card whose sneak cost was paid on an earlier turn returns to hand.",
    "diagnosis": "False positive. The \"this turn\" is carried by the sub-ability's condition `CastVariantPaidInstead { variant: Sneak }`, whose turn scope is intrinsic: `instead_swap_applies` (game/effects/mod.rs:25116-25122) and `evaluate_condition` (game/effects/mod.rs:26313) both compare the object's `cast_variant_paid` with `Some((Sneak, state.turn_number))`, and the sneak cast stamps that pair. The Duration_ThisTurn detector (parser/swallow_check.rs:5367, `detect_duration_this_turn`) only accepts typed carriers whose names contain `ThisTurn` (the AbilityCondition arm at parser/swallow_check.rs:5633-5641) plus an explicit (h2) list, and `AbilityCondition::CastVariantPaidInstead` is in neither, so it reports a swallowed duration; game/coverage.rs:8316 turns every `SwallowedClause` into a `Swallow:{detector}` gap, which marks the card unsupported.",
    "suggested_fix": "In `detect_duration_this_turn` (parser/swallow_check.rs), treat `AbilityCondition::CastVariantPaid { .. }` and `AbilityCondition::CastVariantPaidInstead { .. }` as turn-history carriers, next to the (h2) carriers whose names don't end in `ThisTurn` (their runtime check is `cast_variant_paid == Some((variant, turn_number))`, so the turn scope is part of the condition, CR 702.190a). Alternatively exempt the \"<cost> was paid this turn\" / \"cost was paid this turn\" suffix in `QUANTITY_CONTEXT_SUFFIXES` and confirm it with the typed condition. A regression test: Karai, Future of the Foot parses with no `SwallowedClause` and stays supported in the coverage report.",
    "override_note": "Nothing is patched: the test ops pin the parsed trigger the sandbox games verified (combat damage to a player by Karai, the Graveyard->Hand return of a targeted creature card you own, and the `CastVariantPaidInstead Sneak` sub that moves that same card (ParentTarget) to the battlefield instead). The cases show: the hand branch when Karai was hard cast (her sneak cost was not paid); the sneak branch (cast for {2}{W}{B} during the declare blockers step by returning an unblocked attacker, CR 702.190a; she enters tapped and attacking, CR 702.190b), where her trigger puts the card onto the battlefield instead (CR 608.2c); the same Karai connecting again two turns later returning the card to hand, because the sneak cost was paid on an earlier turn; no trigger when she is blocked (CR 510.3a); and nothing returned when the target leaves the graveyard first (CR 608.2b)."
  },
